Current thesis

AI capability is improving faster than organizations can reliably translate it into real economic work. I believe this makes deployment an increasingly important bottleneck. AI can now begin helping with the search for useful deployment itself, which creates the possibility that deployment becomes more systematic and less dependent on bespoke human work. Lower deployment costs can make more AI use cases economically viable, while real deployment produces friction data that can improve future systems. I do not yet know how large this industry becomes or which architecture ultimately wins. I am investing now because I think the direction of the shift is sufficiently strong to justify an initial position while those questions remain open.

